IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1 (sections 101 to 398) -- THE SHARED VOCABULARY.
--
-- This module is the keel that the eleven pieces (dg1 to dg11) build on.
-- The Law has no interpretation section, so this module encodes no provision of its own:
-- it declares the kinds of person, body and measure that two or more pieces name,
-- and fixes the one way a time limit, an amount, a proportion and a vote are written.
--
-- The source is the plain-text rendering de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt of the Delaware Code Online
-- (through 85 Del. Laws, c. 550), made by a converter script. It is not the official text.
-- Quote lines below are slices of that file: `-- src:N | ...` is line N, and an ellipsis means the line goes on.
--
-- SEAT: a person who incorporates, directs or holds stock in a Delaware corporation
-- (an incorporator, a director or officer, a stockholder including a minority stockholder).
--
-- UNITS, stated once:
--   * an amount of money is a NUMBER of United States dollars: $0.01 is 0.01 and $2,500 is 2500;
--   * a proportion is an exact NUMBER, a fraction of 1: "1/3" is 1 DIVIDED BY 3,
--     "66 2/3%" is (200 DIVIDED BY 3)% (that is, 2 DIVIDED BY 3), "15%" is 15%;
--   * a count of shares, votes, directors or persons is a NUMBER;
--   * a time limit is a Period (below), never a bare NUMBER.
--
-- The files NOTES.md and PROGRESS.md beside this module are the notes the pieces read.

§ `Dialect shim`

-- Not law. The stable build 1.6.98 has no YMD (probe 05 of dialects.md; checked on this binary),
-- so it is defined here, once. A piece must NOT define its own: two definitions of one name
-- cannot be used at all.
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
      m IS A NUMBER
      d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
YMD y m d MEANS Date d m y

§ `Time limits`

-- The Law states its time limits in days, in weeks, in months and in years.
-- src:789 | which record date shall not be more than 60 nor less than 10 days before the date of such meeting …
-- src:561 | by advertisement at least 1 week before the sale …
-- src:1834 | not earlier than 6 months prior to the filing date …
-- src:779 | no such proxy shall be voted or acted upon after 3 years from its date …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 213(a) (src:789); § 164 (src:561); § 371(b)(1) (src:1834); § 212(b) (src:779)
DECLARE `Time unit` IS ONE OF
    `calendar days`
    `calendar weeks`
    `calendar months`
    `calendar years`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 213(a) (src:789); § 164 (src:561); § 371(b)(1) (src:1834); § 212(b) (src:779)
DECLARE Period HAS
    `how many units` IS A NUMBER
    unit             IS A `Time unit`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 213(a) (src:789)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Period
`period in days` n MEANS Period WITH `how many units` IS n, unit IS `calendar days`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 164 (src:561)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Period
`period in weeks` n MEANS Period WITH `how many units` IS n, unit IS `calendar weeks`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 371(b)(1) (src:1834)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Period
`period in months` n MEANS Period WITH `how many units` IS n, unit IS `calendar months`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 212(b) (src:779)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Period
`period in years` n MEANS Period WITH `how many units` IS n, unit IS `calendar years`

-- N days or weeks after D is D plus N calendar days (or 7 times N). N months or years after D is the
-- library's `add months` / `add years`, which clamp to the last day of the target month
-- (31 August plus 6 months is 28 February). Whether the last day is itself inside a period is the
-- piece's reading, not this module's.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 213(a) (src:789); § 371(b)(1) (src:1834); § 212(b) (src:779)
GIVEN p IS A Period
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` p `after` d MEANS
    CONSIDER p's unit
    WHEN `calendar days`   THEN d PLUS p's `how many units`
    WHEN `calendar weeks`  THEN d PLUS (7 TIMES p's `how many units`)
    WHEN `calendar months` THEN `add months` d (p's `how many units`)
    WHEN `calendar years`  THEN `add years` d (p's `how many units`)

@ref 8 Del. C. § 213(a) (src:789); § 164 (src:561); § 371(b)(1) (src:1834)
GIVEN p IS A Period
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` p `before` d MEANS
    CONSIDER p's unit
    WHEN `calendar days`   THEN d MINUS p's `how many units`
    WHEN `calendar weeks`  THEN d MINUS (7 TIMES p's `how many units`)
    WHEN `calendar months` THEN `add months` d (0 MINUS p's `how many units`)
    WHEN `calendar years`  THEN `add years` d (0 MINUS p's `how many units`)

§ `Kinds of corporation and of entity`

-- src:209 | A “charitable nonstock corporation” is any nonprofit nonstock corporation that is exempt from taxation under § 501(c)(3) of the United States Internal Revenue Code [26 U.S.C. § 501(c)(3)], or any successor provisions.
-- src:210 | A “membership interest” is, unless otherwise provided in a nonstock corporation’s certificate of incorporation, a member’s share of the profits and losses of a nonstock corporation, or a member’s right to receive distributions of the nonstock corporation’s assets, or both;
-- src:211 | A “nonprofit nonstock corporation” is a nonstock corporation that does not have membership interests; and
-- src:212 | A “nonstock corporation” is any corporation organized under this chapter that is not authorized to issue capital stock.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 114(d)(1) to (4) (src:209-212)
DECLARE `Kind of corporation` IS ONE OF
    `a stock corporation`
    `a nonstock corporation with membership interests`
    `a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable`
    `a charitable nonstock corporation`

-- The four constructors above are the only ones; the rules below read them. They do not decide the
-- definition: what makes a corporation one kind or another is section 114(d), encoded by dg1.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 114(d)(4) (src:212)
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of corporation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the kind is a stock corporation` k MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `a stock corporation` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

@ref 8 Del. C. § 114(d)(4) (src:212)
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of corporation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the kind is a nonstock corporation` k MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `a stock corporation` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

@ref 8 Del. C. § 114(d)(3) (src:211)
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of corporation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the kind is a nonprofit nonstock corporation` k MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a charitable nonstock corporation` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

@ref 8 Del. C. § 114(d)(1) (src:209)
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of corporation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the kind is a charitable nonstock corporation` k MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `a charitable nonstock corporation` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- src:1832 | the words “foreign corporation” mean a corporation organized under the laws of any jurisdiction other than this State.
-- src:1939 | “Foreign jurisdiction” means any foreign country or other foreign jurisdiction (other than the United States, any state, the District of Columbia, or any possession or territory of the United States); and
@ref 8 Del. C. § 371(a) (src:1832); § 388(a)(1) (src:1939)
DECLARE `Where an entity is formed` IS ONE OF
    `this State`
    `another jurisdiction of the United States`
    `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States`

-- src:660 | “Person” means any individual, corporation, partnership, unincorporated association or other entity.
-- src:1148 | The term “joint-stock association” as used in this section, includes any association of the kind commonly known as a joint-stock association or joint-stock company and any unincorporated association, trust or enterprise having members or having outstanding shares of stock or other evidences of financial or beneficial interest therein, whether formed or organized by agreement or under statutory authority or otherwise and whether formed or organized under the laws of this State or any other jurisdiction, but does not include a corporation, partnership or limited liability company …
-- src:1328 | the term “other entity” means a limited liability company, statutory trust, business trust or association, real estate investment trust, common-law trust or any other unincorporated business including a partnership (whether general (including a limited liability partnership) or limited (including a limited liability limited partnership)), or a foreign corporation.
-- src:1940 | “Non-United States entity” means a corporation, a limited liability company, a statutory trust, a business trust or association, a real estate investment trust, a common-law trust, or any other unincorporated business or entity, including a partnership (whether general (including a limited liability partnership) or limited (including a limited liability limited partnership)), formed, incorporated, created or that otherwise came into being under the laws of any foreign jurisdiction.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(c)(6) (src:660); § 254(a) (src:1148); § 265(a) (src:1328); § 388(a)(2) (src:1940)
DECLARE `Kind of entity` IS ONE OF
    `a natural person`
    `a corporation` HAS `its kind` IS A `Kind of corporation`
    `a general partnership`
    `a limited partnership`
    `a limited liability partnership`
    `a limited liability limited partnership`
    `a limited liability company`
    `a statutory trust`
    `a business trust or association`
    `a real estate investment trust`
    `a common-law trust`
    `a joint-stock association`
    `any other unincorporated business or association`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 265(a) (src:1328); § 388(a)(2) (src:1940)
DECLARE Entity HAS
    `kind of entity` IS A `Kind of entity`
    `where formed`   IS A `Where an entity is formed`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 371(a) (src:1832)
GIVEN e IS AN Entity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the entity was formed under the laws of this State` e MEANS
    e's `where formed` EQUALS `this State`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 371(a) (src:1832)
GIVEN e IS AN Entity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the entity was formed under the laws of a jurisdiction other than this State` e MEANS
    NOT (e's `where formed` EQUALS `this State`)

@ref 8 Del. C. § 388(a)(1) (src:1939)
GIVEN e IS AN Entity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the entity was formed under the laws of a foreign jurisdiction` e MEANS
    e's `where formed` EQUALS `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States`

§ `Who acts, and where a provision is made`

-- src:130 | the incorporator or incorporators, until the directors are elected, shall manage the affairs of the corporation and may do whatever is necessary and proper to perfect the organization of the corporation, including the adoption of the original bylaws of the corporation and the election of directors.
-- src:363 | shall be managed by or under the direction of a board of directors, except as may be otherwise provided in this chapter or in its certificate of incorporation. If any such provision is made in the certificate of incorporation, the powers and duties conferred or imposed upon the board of directors by this chapter shall be exercised or performed to such extent and by such person or persons as shall be provided in the certificate of incorporation.
-- src:383 | Every corporation organized under this chapter shall have such officers with such titles and duties as shall be stated in the bylaws or in a resolution of the board of directors which is not inconsistent with the bylaws and as may be necessary to enable it to sign instruments and stock certificates which comply with §§ 103(a)(2) and 158 of this title. One of the officers shall have the duty to record the proceedings of the meetings of the stockholders and directors in a book to be kept for that purpose. Any number of offices may be held by the same person unless the certificate of incorporation or bylaws otherwise provide.
-- src:436 | is or was a director, officer, employee or agent of the corporation, or is or was serving at the request of the corporation as a director, officer, employee or agent of another corporation, partnership, joint venture, trust or other enterprise, against expenses (including attorneys’ fees), judgments, fines and amounts paid in settlement actually and reasonably incurred by the person in connection with such action, suit or proceeding if the person acted in good faith and in a manner the person reasonably believed to be in or not opposed to the best interests of the corporation, and, with respect to any criminal action or proceeding, had no reasonable cause to believe the person’s conduct was unlawful. The termination of any action, suit or proceeding by judgment, order, settlement, conviction, or upon a plea of nolo contendere or its equivalent, shall not, of itself, create a presumption that the person did not act in good faith and in a manner which the person reasonably believed to be in or not opposed to the best interests of the corporation, and, with respect to any criminal action or proceeding, had reasonable cause to believe that the person’s conduct was unlawful.
-- src:779 | Each stockholder entitled to vote at a meeting of stockholders or to express consent or dissent to corporate action in writing without a meeting may authorize another person or persons to act for such stockholder by proxy, but no such proxy shall be voted or acted upon after 3 years from its date, unless the proxy provides for a longer period.
-- src:196 | All references to stockholders of the corporation shall be deemed to refer to members of the corporation;
-- src:566 | except with the consent of all other subscribers or the corporation, for a period of 6 months from its date.
-- src:768 | stockholders and proxyholders not physically present at a meeting of stockholders may, by means of remote communication:
-- src:302 | Every corporation shall have and maintain in this State a registered agent, which agent may be any of:
-- src:1523 | the Court of Chancery, on the application of any creditor or stockholder thereof, may, at any time, appoint 1 or more persons to be receivers …
-- src:1461 | appoint 1 or more of the directors of the corporation to be trustees, or appoint 1 or more persons to be receivers, of and for the corporation, to take charge of the corporation’s property, and to collect the debts and property due and belonging to the corporation, with power to prosecute and defend, in the name of the corporation, or otherwise, all such suits as may be necessary or proper for the purposes aforesaid, and to appoint an agent or agents under them, and to do all other acts which might be done by the corporation, if in being, that may be necessary for the final settlement of the unfinished business of the corporation. The powers of the trustees or receivers may be continued as long as the Court of Chancery shall think necessary for the purposes aforesaid.
-- src:921 | may appoint 1 or more persons to be custodians, and, if the corporation is insolvent, to be receivers, of and for any corporation when:
-- src:954 | appoint 1 or more inspectors to act at the meeting and make a written report thereof. The corporation may designate 1 or more persons as alternate inspectors to replace any inspector who fails to act. If no inspector or alternate is able to act at a meeting of stockholders, the person presiding at the meeting shall appoint 1 or more inspectors to act at the meeting. Each inspector, before entering upon the discharge of the duties of inspector, shall take and sign an oath faithfully to execute the duties of inspector with strict impartiality and according to the best of such inspector’s ability.
-- src:80 | Whenever any instrument is to be filed with the Secretary of State or in accordance with this section or chapter, such instrument shall be executed as follows:
-- src:277 | In a proceeding by the Attorney General to dissolve the corporation, or to enjoin the corporation from the transaction of unauthorized business.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 107 (src:130); § 141(a) (src:363); § 142(a) (src:383); § 145(a) (src:436); § 212(b) (src:779); § 114(a)(1) (src:196); § 165 (src:566); § 211(a)(2) (src:768); § 132(a) (src:302); § 291 (src:1523); § 279 (src:1461); § 226(a) (src:921); § 231(a) (src:954); § 103(a) (src:80); § 124(3) (src:277)
DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    `the corporation`
